      "content": "okay but what if she wasn't being \"obvious\" with the rouge or the big dresses? like if someone actually lived for a long time they'd probably learn how to blend in. \n\ni've been reading about her later years and how she was known for being incredibly poised even under extreme pressure. i noticed this woman today didn't just have \"royal aesthetics,\" she had this specific way of sitting where she never actually touches the back of the chair, almost like she's staying ready to move. it was so precise. \n\ncan you look into any accounts of her mannerisms or specific physical habits? like, beyond just clothes, were there any known idiosyncrasies in how she held herself or gestured that might be passed down or even mimicked by someone who actually knew her? i want to see if there's a behavioral \"fingerprint\" i can look for.",
